# INV-02 — invented. Four overs a side, the first innings defended by one run.
# Edge cases: a wide with a run (odd: the batters change ends); no-balls with
# runs off the bat and a four off one; the free hit after a front-foot
# no-ball — a bowled that does not stand on it, and a run out that does (with
# a wide between the no-ball and the free hit, which leaves the free hit
# due); a maiden with a leg bye in it; caught and bowled; hit wicket; byes;
# a chase that ends its overs one short of a tie.
match INV-02
title Four overs, defended by one run
date 2026-11-02
overs 4
sides Home Away

innings 1 Home
open B1 B2
over BW1  wd+1 1 nb+2 W:b 3 . 2 .
over BW2  4 nb+4 wd W:ro/F5,+1,end=s 6 1 . 1
over BW1  . . 1lb . . .
over BW2  W:c/F2 1 W:cb 4 2 .

innings 2 Away
open B1 B2
over BW1  1 2 . 4 1 .
over BW2  W:hw . 2 nb 1 wd 6 .
over BW3  1 1 4 W:lbw . 2
over BW1  1 2b 4 . 1 2

# ── The card, worked by hand ──
# Home: 11, 19, 1 (the maiden's leg bye), 7 = 38. B1 is not out on the free
# hit (bowled), and out on the next free hit (run out, which stands).
card 1
bat B1 14 6 2 0 run out (F5)
bat B2 4 10 0 0 c F2 b BW2
bat B3 7 6 0 1 c&b BW2
bat B4 1 1 0 0 not out
bat B5 6 3 1 0 not out
extras b 0 lb 1 w 3 nb 2 p 0
total 38/3 4.0
fow 1-22 B1 1.2
fow 2-31 B2 3.1
fow 3-32 B3 3.3
bowl BW1 2-1-11-0 wd 1 nb 1
bowl BW2 2-0-26-2 wd 1 nb 1

# Away, needing 39: 8, 11, 8, 10 = 37 in four overs.
card 2
bat B1 11 7 0 1 not out
bat B2 7 5 1 0 hit wicket b BW2
bat B3 8 7 1 0 lbw b BW3
bat B4 7 6 1 0 not out
extras b 2 lb 0 w 1 nb 1 p 0
total 37/2 4.0
fow 1-8 B2 1.1
fow 2-25 B3 2.4
bowl BW1 2-0-16-0 wd 0 nb 0
bowl BW2 1-0-11-1 wd 1 nb 1
bowl BW3 1-0-8-1 wd 0 nb 0

result Home won by 1 run
